{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJgs41B5cffqzZ6rub3v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both tests pass now (`Ran 2 tests ... OK`).\n\n**Why it crashed:** the report itself was fine. `ingest/reader.py` was reading the CSV with `delimiter=\";\"`, but the sales exports use commas. That's what the file's own header comment says, and `data/sales.csv` matches it. So each line came back as one column named `\"shop,amount\"`, and looking up `r[\"amount\"]` raised a `KeyError`.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `ingest/reader.py`: removed `delimiter=\";\"` so it uses the standard comma.\n- `analytics/stats.py`: set `UNIT = \"CLP\"`.\n\nThe crash fix is in the ingest module, not the analytics code. I changed it there because that's where the bug was, rather than working around it in the report. But it affects anything else that calls `rows()`, so the ingest owner may want to review it. If some shops do upload semicolon-separated files, the reader needs to detect the delimiter instead of assuming one. `csv.Sniffer` can do that.\n\nNothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":764,"cache_read_input_tokens":22710,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":764},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38711ba8-26e5-47e7-bf30-f7878602f195","uuid":"14698216-ce8d-4eca-b8d9-246024ff7f34","timestamp":"2026-10-23T06:22:50.505Z","request_id":"req_011CgJgs3iJgeWrk7ypaAdQ2"}
